Question:

Hi all,

  We have two alpha stations 2000 with OSF1 V3.0 and we want
  to change the default timezone of the system to GMT0.

  Now we are using the TZ envirnment variable for each user.
  I used /usr/sbin/timezone to chanege the system default timezone,
  but it did not work.

  When a type date it shows:

    Wed Feb 21 16:12:15 MET 1996

  and with date -u it shows:

    Wed Feb 21 15:20:20 UTC 1996

  And we wish

    Wed Feb 21 16:12:15 GMT 1996

  Could anyone help me ?
  TIA


Answer:


On Wed, 21 Feb 1996, Herve DEMARTHE wrote:

> Javier,
> 
> Try this :
> 
> cd /etc/zoneinfo
> ln -s ./GMT+0 localtime
> date
> 
> It worked for me (I am in the MET zone).
> I have :
> 
> timezone        0 dst 0
> 
> in /sys/conf/MACHINE (system config file)
> 
> Hope this helps,
> Regards,

It did, thanks.

