> My original post was:
> 
> > I'm trying to run Netscape 2.0 on our Alpha under DU 3.2 but with the -display
> > aimed at an Ultrix 4.4 MIPS workstation.  Netscape 1.12 works fine in this mode,
> > but Netscape 2.0 segmentation faults before any window appears on the X server 
> > and with no indication on stderr of what the problem is.  I've sent Netscape a
> > report, but of course they may never get around to responding.  Any thoughts?
> 
> I received several replies.  The consensus was that the version of X Windows
> that came with Ultrix 4.4 is old enough that it probably is incompatible with
> Netscape 2.0.  The recommended solution is to install a later version of X on
> the Ultrix box.  Although I haven't done this yet, it sound like good advice
> to me.  Thanks to all concerned.

After I issued the first summary, several people wrote to say they had
situations similar to mine and had no problem.  I cannot explain that.

I did some further tests: I tried running Netscape 2.0 on the DU 3.2
box but instead of my Ultrix 4.4 workstation as the X server, I used a
colleague's RS6000 workstation.  Netscape issued a complaint about not finding
some font and then it again dropped core with a segmentation fault.

I then found a different platform with a Netscape 2.0 on it.  This is an
HP9000/735 running HP-UX.  I ran Netscape there with my original Ultrix
workstation as the X server.  It works fine.

My conclusion: there is something wrong with the DU binary for Netscape 2.0
that prevents it from running in this mode - something that was NOT wrong with
Netscape 1.12.

For now, I'm using the HP for Netscape.  What's the world coming to?

							Steve Campbell

