After reading all these responses and taking your advice into consideration,  I 
had no problems at all:

	renamed /sys/conf/BAD-NAME to /sys/conf/GOOD-NAME
	renamed /sys/conf/BAD-NAME.list to /sys/conf/GOOD-NAME.list
	renamed /sys/BAD-NAME to /sys/GOOD-NAME
	editted /etc/rc.config and changed the HOSTNAME to GOOD-NAME
	[held breath]
	rebooted

Luckily for me this system is stand-alone at present and there were no email or 
network configuration files that needed to be changed.

		
