From tru64-unix-managers  Tue Feb 20 09:45:52 1996
From: Julyan Cartwright <julyan () hp1 ! uib ! es>
Date: Tue, 20 Feb 1996 09:45:52 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: CDE keyboard problem
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96076329121389

I wanted to know how to tell CDE about the Spanish keyboards 
on our alphas. I asked:

> How do I tell CDE that we have Spanish keyboards on our Alphas? I've got as 
> far as working out I need to set the LC_CTYPE environment variable, but when 
> I run locale -a I get
> POSIX
> en_US.ISO8859-1
> as the only choices. So where do I get the information to set this to some
> other value? Also, how do I get other choices apart from 'C' to appear in 
> the list in the login screen?

It turned out to be simple - just make sure the 
link /var/X11/xdm/keymap_default is set to the correct keymap. 
Many thanks to Tom Woodburn of the CDE team at DEC for that 
insight. Thanks also to the others who offered me advice. 
I was, and still am, a little confused about what locales and environment 
variables like LC_CTYPE are for, if not for changing the keyboard settings 
I suppose they change the language in which menus appear, etc?

Finally, I'd like to congratulate the CDE team at DEC for an excellent 
product - now our users prefer using our Alphas screens to our HPs running
VUE!
	Julyan
