From tru64-unix-managers  Mon Feb 19 22:33:15 1996
From: Michel Cyr <cyrmiche () sidoci ! qc ! ca>
Date: Mon, 19 Feb 1996 22:33:15 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: CDDI + Turbo Channel = No Reboot
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96076329121385

Thank's to everyone who took the time to answer my request(s) !

Many pointed out that i was using the wrong syntax at the console
prompt. But this was not the real problem. This was a way to reproduce
the problem. Firmware 6.0 let you use lowercase with the "fi flag" of
the console boot command. (6.4 doesn't let you do so anymore !!!)

The real problem was that, under normal operation (booted kernel =
vmunix), if a crash of the OS occured or if the command "reboot" was
typed; the system would HANG with :

...

INIT-S-MEM...
INIT-S-NVR...
INIT-S-SCC...
INIT-S-NI...
INIT-S-SCSI...
INIT-S-ISDN...
AUDIT_BOOT_STARTS ... 
AUDIT_CHECKSUM_GOOD
AUDIT_LOAD_BEGINS
AUDIT_LOAD_DONE

OSF boot - Mon Jul 24 21:56:39 EDT 1995

can't open VMUNIX
Enter [kernel_name] [option_1 ... option_n]:

Waiting for you to type the name of the kernel. A return at that post
is OK !


AXP Firmware upgrade to 6.4 AND PMAF-FU to 3.0U solved that one !

A TIP : If you install a 100 Mbits DEFTA-UA make sure you have
	Firmware update 3.4 not too far. If you don't, than just hard
	link /VMUNIX to /vmunix till you find the CD.

--
