On Tue, 13 Feb 96 22:42:33 MST, I wrote:

>Hello,
>	I'm running DU 3.2A on a 250 4/266. I have a problem that is
>probably really easy but I haven't found any documentation about it.
>ftpd is not allowing any connections. Prompts for user name, then
>password, and then login fails. Even when the correct passwd is entered.
>/etc/shells, /etc/ftpusers exist and are correct, and I'm not running
>ENHANCED security.

The problem was that ftpd was being started as daemon instead of as root.
>From inetd.conf:
ftp  stream  tcp   nowait    root    /usr/sbin/ftpd    ftpd

That is the correct entry. I had daemon instead of root.
Also, as many people pointed out, the fact that it uses audgen shows I'm
running enhanced security. Though, when I do a secsetup and select BASE
security it tells me it's already running base. I'll figure that out
later.

