From: Gerhard Kircher <kircher@edvz.tuwien.ac.at>

Well here is my /sbin/init.d/local:

#!/sbin/sh
# 

PATH=/sbin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin
export PATH

case "$1" in
'start')
        [ -x /usr/local/sbin/sshd ] && /usr/local/sbin/sshd
        echo "sshd - secure shell daemon"
        ;;
'stop')
        ;;
*)
        echo "usage: $0 {start|stop}"
        ;;
esac

The  differences  are:  1)  you are using /bin/sh instead of
/sbin/sh and 2) you don't set PATH  so  echo  might  not  be
found.

