Subject: setld new installtion results
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96076329121268

Many thanks for all the replies to my question about having to delete
a previous version of a product before installing a new version.

The concensus was that a "good" setld install procedure should perform
this function automatically.  Some do, some don't.  A good setld script
takes a significant amount of time to perfect, so some developers scrimp
on a quality script. (Note: No installs I've found will let you re-install
the current version, without first deleting the current version.  There is
no - "do it again option" for setld.  You might want to do this if you
suspect one of the files is corrupt for instance.)

