Hi

My summary for the above is :

Run the XIsso -is an X application in /usr/tcb/bin- that manages all about
accounts in C2-sec. 
When you get the window, go to "Accounts". 
Then go to "Modify User Accounts". 
There, ask for the account you want to disallow the password history, and when 
you have it, put the "Password History Limit" in 0.
After this, the account will be able to re-use old passwords.


My original question is :

> Is there any way to change a user password under C2 security without
> caring about what is the previous passwords ?  This is because the C2
> security does not allows a user to change to a previously used password.
>

